# Backspace String Compare — LeetCode 844

**Pattern:** Two Pointers  
**Approach:** Traverse both strings from right to left.

## Approach
1. Initialize `i = s.length() - 1` and `j = t.length() - 1`.
2. Use a `back` counter to track pending backspaces.
3. `#` increments `back`; a normal character with `back > 0` is skipped and decrements `back`.
4. Compare the next valid characters of both strings.
5. If they differ, return `false`.
6. If both pointers finish, return `true`.

## Java Code

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean backspaceCompare(String s, String t) {
        int i = s.length() - 1;
        int j = t.length() - 1;

        while (true) {
            int back = 0;

            while (i >= 0 && (s.charAt(i) == '#' || back > 0)) {
                if (s.charAt(i) == '#')
                    back++;
                else
                    back--;
                i--;
            }

            back = 0;

            while (j >= 0 && (t.charAt(j) == '#' || back > 0)) {
                if (t.charAt(j) == '#')
                    back++;
                else
                    back--;
                j--;
            }

            if (i >= 0 && j >= 0 && s.charAt(i) == t.charAt(j)) {
                i--;
                j--;
            } else {
                break;
            }
        }

        return i == -1 && j == -1;
    }
}
